WEBVTT

01:29.980 --> 01:32.980
<b>San'yadori 
Festival</b>

01:33.190 --> 01:35.990
Episode 8: C'mere, You Want Some Free Candy?

01:39.070 --> 01:41.990
<b>Muramatsuya</b>

01:43.590 --> 01:46.000
Right. I understand.

01:47.520 --> 01:49.340
Yes, please do.

01:50.150 --> 01:51.680
I'll be waiting.

01:56.310 --> 01:58.580
I'm sorry you came here 
just for this to happen.

01:59.040 --> 02:01.950
The police will be here soon, 
so perhaps you should...

02:32.470 --> 02:34.890
This isn't another riddle for me to solve.

02:35.460 --> 02:39.380
Osanai-san's been abducted. 
The police are getting involved.

02:40.240 --> 02:42.300
This isn't one for me.

02:51.570 --> 02:52.600
Osanai-san!

02:53.280 --> 02:54.620
<i>"I'm sorry."</i>

02:53.320 --> 02:59.820
I'm sorry

02:53.320 --> 02:59.820
Please buy four candy apples and a canelé

02:53.320 --> 02:59.820
I'm sorry

02:54.620 --> 02:58.560
<i>"Please buy four candy apples and a canelé."</i>

02:58.560 --> 02:59.830
<i>"I'm sorry."</i>

03:05.070 --> 03:10.830
<i>The number you have dialed is outside
the service area or is switched off.</i>

03:29.140 --> 03:29.980
<i>What is it?</i>

03:29.980 --> 03:32.070
Kengo. Come over right away.

03:32.070 --> 03:34.100
<i>Want another extra spicy tanmen?</i>

03:34.100 --> 03:36.130
Osanai-san's been abducted.

03:36.130 --> 03:38.770
Her kidnapper's demanding a ransom.

03:38.770 --> 03:41.300
And Osanai-san just sent me a message.

03:41.300 --> 03:43.780
I'm gonna find out where 
she is and call the police.

03:43.780 --> 03:45.520
Please, come give me a hand.

03:45.520 --> 03:47.960
<i>Jogoro. That's not funny.</i>

03:47.960 --> 03:50.460
I'm not joking. It's true.

03:50.460 --> 03:53.130
The police are heading 
to Osanai-san's place now.

03:53.130 --> 03:55.680
<i>Don't you have anyone else you can ask?</i>

03:55.680 --> 03:56.620
No, I don't!

04:01.630 --> 04:04.640
<b>Kobato Japanese Confectionery</b>

04:11.880 --> 04:13.020
What's this?

04:13.020 --> 04:16.070
Only Osanai-san and I have this map.

04:16.400 --> 04:21.230
It's a special map she made
listing all the sweets shops across town.

04:21.610 --> 04:24.650
And this is the message she sent me.

04:25.870 --> 04:28.040
Just one canelé?

04:28.040 --> 04:29.620
Is it odd that it's just one?

04:30.250 --> 04:32.990
The canelés I know are tiny.

04:32.990 --> 04:34.500
Why would she want just one?

04:35.050 --> 04:36.760
I thought so.

04:37.430 --> 04:39.660
This isn't just an errand request.

04:40.130 --> 04:41.350
Look at this.

04:41.350 --> 04:44.340
This is the shop that sells candy apples.

04:43.550 --> 04:49.560
<b>Muramatsuya</b>

04:45.130 --> 04:47.210
Muramatsuya's candy apples.

04:47.210 --> 04:51.200
The next stop on Osanai's 
Summer Sweets Selection.

04:51.200 --> 04:52.390
Say what?

04:54.060 --> 04:58.000
And the canelés are listed at...

04:58.320 --> 05:00.820
<b>Lemon Seed</b>

04:58.320 --> 05:00.820
<b>Canelés</b>

04:59.110 --> 05:00.460
Lemon Seed.

05:05.560 --> 05:07.360
Found it. Here.

05:05.570 --> 05:07.950
<b>Lemon Seed</b>

05:08.290 --> 05:11.330
Osanai-san gave me a riddle a while back.

05:11.330 --> 05:11.790
<b>Laroche</b>

05:11.750 --> 05:15.830
She listed two shops and asked me 
to meet her between them.

05:12.700 --> 05:13.450
<b>Ginsendo</b>

05:13.450 --> 05:15.830
<b>Laroche</b>

05:13.450 --> 05:15.830
<b>Ginsendo</b>

05:13.450 --> 05:15.830
<b>Berry Berry
at San'yadori</b>

05:16.560 --> 05:19.830
By that logic, she'd be around here.

05:19.840 --> 05:22.340
<b>Remora Akanebe</b>

05:20.680 --> 05:22.340
It's a shopping mall.

05:22.830 --> 05:24.570
Why? It'd be crowded.

05:26.550 --> 05:28.870
That's where the quantities come in.

05:30.860 --> 05:32.360
We have to apply what we know.

05:40.840 --> 05:42.170
Four to one.

05:42.800 --> 05:44.640
Four from Muramatsuya.

05:44.640 --> 05:46.670
One from Lemon Seed.

05:47.740 --> 05:49.740
<b>Nanbu Gymnasium</b>

05:48.490 --> 05:49.350
Here.

05:49.730 --> 05:51.480
Nanbu Gymnasium?

05:51.800 --> 05:54.330
Huh? Was that not it?

05:54.330 --> 05:58.120
Jogoro, didn't you know? 
That place is being rebuilt.

05:58.510 --> 06:01.170
It's a giant, locked-down derelict right now.

06:44.720 --> 06:46.060
Here, maybe?

07:02.860 --> 07:04.130
It's perfectly clean.

07:04.510 --> 07:06.700
Someone must have driven it here recently.

07:07.400 --> 07:09.960
Maybe the back door's been left open.

07:32.930 --> 07:34.470
What's up, Jogoro?

07:34.470 --> 07:35.510
Over there.

07:35.510 --> 07:38.870
I'm not sure, but it looks 
like a lollipop wrapper.

07:39.520 --> 07:40.720
A lollipop?

07:41.200 --> 07:42.790
Candy on a stick.

07:43.450 --> 07:45.740
Osanai-san has them sometimes.

07:46.730 --> 07:50.400
She'd better not have gone off
with someone offering her candy.

07:51.330 --> 07:53.410
That's not funny, Kengo.

07:53.410 --> 07:54.350
Sorry.

07:54.850 --> 07:56.360
So are you certain?

07:57.490 --> 07:59.210
Not yet.

08:09.290 --> 08:11.210
Kengo, what do you think that is?

08:15.270 --> 08:17.140
I've seen one somewhere before.

08:17.990 --> 08:20.320
I think it's a voice changer.

08:22.320 --> 08:27.130
The call Osanai-san's mother 
received was through a machine.

08:27.860 --> 08:29.030
Should we call the police?

08:31.260 --> 08:33.770
Let's make sure Osanai-san's here first.

08:35.540 --> 08:40.300
If the front passenger seat was empty
 and she was in the back,

08:40.300 --> 08:41.970
there must've been multiple people.

08:42.540 --> 08:45.570
At least two. Probably three.

08:45.570 --> 08:46.810
Let's be careful.

08:48.340 --> 08:50.650
What now? Smash a window and go inside?

08:50.650 --> 08:53.400
No, I don't want them to know we're here.

08:55.920 --> 08:57.070
That door.

08:58.510 --> 08:59.460
Let's go.

09:26.850 --> 09:27.710
What is it?

09:28.330 --> 09:29.220
Look.

09:54.270 --> 09:56.780
You can't be serious.

09:56.780 --> 09:57.420
Jogoro.

09:58.060 --> 10:00.790
She's beyond useless. Total trash.

10:00.790 --> 10:02.260
I know.

10:02.260 --> 10:03.380
Voices.

10:03.380 --> 10:05.150
Yeah. What now?

10:05.570 --> 10:09.410
We've come this far. Let's get a look 
at Osanai-san before we call the police.

10:10.260 --> 10:14.740
She was the one who was trying to get cozy, 
and now she wants to bail. What a brat.

10:15.050 --> 10:18.440
Gonna kill Sanae the next time I see her.

10:18.440 --> 10:21.270
Sweet idea. Bet she's gonna cry again.

10:21.580 --> 10:24.930
She was so terrified of that wrench 
last time. That was hilarious.

10:24.930 --> 10:27.070
It's Sanae's own fault, though.

10:27.070 --> 10:30.270
She's stewing in her own jaws.

10:30.740 --> 10:31.770
You mean "juices"?

10:31.770 --> 10:33.410
Oh, is that the phrase?

10:37.210 --> 10:38.750
Seriously?

10:43.160 --> 10:48.120
Either way, <i>you're</i> the worst one.

10:48.120 --> 10:53.110
You look so docile, 
but you've really done it.

10:53.110 --> 10:54.600
It was you, wasn't it?

10:58.350 --> 11:00.040
Don't just sit there.

11:00.550 --> 11:05.900
I got put on probation 
because you ratted me out.

11:05.900 --> 11:09.320
And you're still gonna act 
like it's not your problem?

11:09.320 --> 11:14.330
Grovel and beg Hasemi for
 forgiveness. Say you did it.

11:14.330 --> 11:17.910
Yeah. Hurry up and get down on your knees.

11:17.910 --> 11:19.310
Come on.

11:19.650 --> 11:22.320
Say something, yeah?

11:26.390 --> 11:28.340
You piss me off. You know that?

11:29.760 --> 11:32.030
Like, seriously.

11:39.200 --> 11:41.440
<i>Hello, Osanai here.</i>

11:41.440 --> 11:44.760
Hello. I'm Kobato. From earlier.

11:44.760 --> 11:46.310
We found Yuki-san.

11:47.480 --> 11:49.280
She's at the Nanbu Gymnasium.

11:49.280 --> 11:52.160
In the martial arts room 
at the closed Nanbu Gymnasium.

11:52.160 --> 11:55.050
The kidnappers are a group 
of five girls, all high school age.

11:56.090 --> 11:57.610
Are the police there?

11:57.610 --> 11:59.110
Who are you?

11:59.570 --> 12:01.610
Is what you just said true?

12:06.160 --> 12:08.790
I'm Kobato Jogoro.

12:08.790 --> 12:10.620
I'm Osanai Yuki-san's friend.

12:11.000 --> 12:14.410
I had a hunch where she might be
 and went looking for her.

12:14.970 --> 12:18.910
Osanai-san's currently tied up 
and surrounded by her kidnappers.

12:19.460 --> 12:20.640
Please come quickly.

12:20.640 --> 12:22.420
<i>Nanbu Gymnasium, correct?</i>

12:22.420 --> 12:23.380
Yes.

12:23.690 --> 12:26.560
<i>Understood. We'll be there in five minutes.</i>

12:26.560 --> 12:28.020
Thanks.

12:33.790 --> 12:35.430
My nerves...

12:35.980 --> 12:39.140
Jogoro, did you see the girl 
who was interrogating her?

12:39.140 --> 12:41.160
Yeah, I did.

12:41.160 --> 12:43.280
That was Isawa Hasemi.

12:43.280 --> 12:44.330
I'm sure of it.

12:44.920 --> 12:46.220
Isn't Isawa...

12:46.220 --> 12:48.380
The one who dragged 
Kawamata Sanae into their group.

12:48.810 --> 12:50.920
The leader of the drug group.

12:52.270 --> 12:55.710
From what I've heard, 
Isawa's pretty messed up.

12:55.710 --> 12:57.540
We don't know what she might do.

13:00.040 --> 13:02.640
I'll spare your face.

13:02.640 --> 13:04.790
How about you put your arm out?

13:06.840 --> 13:09.940
Aw, Hasemi, you're too kind.

13:10.610 --> 13:12.770
Feel like apologizing now?

13:14.260 --> 13:15.720
Although...

13:15.720 --> 13:18.280
I won't be stopping now, either way.

13:19.720 --> 13:20.570
Let's go.

13:21.470 --> 13:22.490
Hey!

13:40.710 --> 13:42.200
Isawa-san.

13:42.200 --> 13:46.610
Five slaps. One punch to 
the shoulder. One to the arm.

13:46.610 --> 13:49.340
A horrible punch to the stomach.

13:49.340 --> 13:51.320
Two kicks to the shin.

13:51.320 --> 13:54.340
Another to the knee 
that was aimed at the shin.

13:54.990 --> 13:56.130
And...

13:56.650 --> 14:00.560
Tugging my hair once 
even after I said it hurt.

14:01.560 --> 14:04.270
And the person behind me: Hojo-san.

14:05.140 --> 14:09.300
She suggested tying me up
even though she knew I couldn't run away.

14:09.300 --> 14:14.590
I'm tied up so tight right now, 
I have no sensation in my fingers.

14:15.550 --> 14:16.730
But it's fine.

14:17.200 --> 14:19.600
It hurt, but it's fine.

14:20.030 --> 14:23.770
It hurt inside my mouth 
a little, but it's fine.

14:23.770 --> 14:26.420
It doesn't bother me. So don't worry.

14:27.420 --> 14:28.420
But...

14:28.680 --> 14:32.590
If you hurt me with that, 
you'll leave a mark.

14:33.300 --> 14:35.900
Think about what happens then.

14:36.380 --> 14:38.180
You get it, don't you?

14:40.540 --> 14:46.380
If that happens, I'll probably end up 
being reminded every time I see it.

14:46.790 --> 14:49.440
About you, Isawa-san.

14:50.020 --> 14:52.560
And Hojo-san.

14:53.460 --> 14:54.580
Ueno-san.

14:55.040 --> 14:56.230
Soda-san.

14:56.750 --> 14:57.840
Hayashi-san.

14:59.210 --> 15:01.790
I don't think I'll ever 
be able to forget you.

15:05.380 --> 15:06.460
So?

15:10.190 --> 15:13.520
So what if you remember me?

15:13.520 --> 15:17.380
Why don't I make it easier 
for you to remember?

15:20.200 --> 15:21.960
Wanna try the throat?

15:24.060 --> 15:26.080
Careful how you move or you'll die.

15:26.080 --> 15:27.900
Hah, although...

15:28.240 --> 15:31.560
Maybe you're better off dead!

15:32.400 --> 15:33.920
That's enough, moron.

15:39.920 --> 15:41.370
Um...

15:44.710 --> 15:47.200
You don't want any more on your record.

15:51.000 --> 15:52.230
Who are you?

15:52.230 --> 15:53.730
Strangers.

15:53.730 --> 15:55.220
Oh, him, too.

15:55.220 --> 15:56.660
Get lost.

15:56.660 --> 15:58.720
We're in the middle of a chat.

15:59.380 --> 16:00.980
A chat?

16:02.410 --> 16:03.590
Try being funnier.

16:10.700 --> 16:12.400
Don't touch me!

16:12.400 --> 16:15.060
I told you I'm the victim here!

16:23.010 --> 16:24.870
Yeah. It's me.

16:25.340 --> 16:26.490
I'm not hurt.

16:28.120 --> 16:30.570
They want to hear from me tomorrow.

16:32.050 --> 16:36.160
Sorry. The police will give me a ride home.

16:40.010 --> 16:43.190
Kobato-kun. Does it hurt? Are you all right?

16:44.250 --> 16:46.630
It's nothing compared to what Kengo took.

16:48.090 --> 16:51.090
I have to thank Dojima-kun, too.

16:51.090 --> 16:54.370
He left in an ambulance. 
It'll have to be another time.

16:57.320 --> 16:59.150
I hope he's okay.

16:59.150 --> 17:02.100
Ah, it couldn't have been 
more than a few scrapes.

17:02.530 --> 17:04.180
Are you okay, though?

17:04.180 --> 17:06.660
You heard that, huh?

17:08.520 --> 17:10.890
I'm actually hurting all over.

17:11.500 --> 17:14.810
She doesn't hold back when she hits me.

17:15.960 --> 17:16.960
Yeah?

17:17.420 --> 17:19.340
Shall we be off?

17:19.870 --> 17:20.790
Okay.

17:22.770 --> 17:25.470
Thanks for coming, Kobato-kun.

17:26.170 --> 17:29.470
I had a feeling you'd come.

17:29.930 --> 17:34.700
That reckless trash talk was only 
because you knew I was there, wasn't it?

17:35.120 --> 17:39.160
I never expected you to 
burst in like that, though.

17:40.590 --> 17:43.100
I thought I was buying time.

17:53.310 --> 17:55.640
Thank you very much.

17:55.640 --> 17:57.560
Ah, um...

17:58.460 --> 18:00.180
You're welcome.

18:04.060 --> 18:06.470
What's wrong? Is it where you got hit?

18:06.470 --> 18:08.560
That's part of it, but...

18:09.110 --> 18:10.780
I'm hungry.

18:14.030 --> 18:15.750
Hey, Osanai-san.

18:16.120 --> 18:17.840
You've had a rough day.

18:18.360 --> 18:22.150
I'll buy something you like 
and bring it over to your place.

18:24.260 --> 18:28.260
It's fine. I should be 
the one buying you gifts.

18:28.530 --> 18:32.510
Nah, you can do that later. 
This is something different.

18:32.510 --> 18:35.500
Really? In that case...

18:35.500 --> 18:39.770
Let's make it the next stop on
Osanai's Summer Sweets Selection.

18:40.030 --> 18:41.300
Your next one was...

18:42.660 --> 18:44.520
Tinker Linker's peach pie!

18:45.090 --> 18:49.040
They use white peaches.
 It's really, <i>really</i> delicious.

18:52.320 --> 18:55.610
All right. I'll go buy some peach pie.

18:56.000 --> 18:57.270
Thanks.

18:57.830 --> 19:02.890
All that's left now is 
Cecilia's summer tropical parfait.

19:05.290 --> 19:08.290
<b>Kobato Japanese Confectionery</b>

19:12.550 --> 19:15.550
Osanai's Top 10!

19:12.550 --> 19:15.550
Cecilia

19:12.550 --> 19:15.550
 Summer Tropical Parfait

19:12.550 --> 19:15.550
Tinker Linker

19:12.550 --> 19:15.550
Peach Pie

